From 01cb2fed8a84cdff923535b7d050974720c25c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nx-on-orbis <nx-on-orbis@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:45:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] PS4: staging buffer cap and GPU memory reclaim before
 failing, from Eden4

From Eden4 (github.com/xatyy/Eden4, GPL-3.0-or-later):
- staging buffers are capped at 64 MiB; above that the renderer waits for
  the GPU and reuses or frees idle ones instead of allocating more;
- every staging level is released every frame (upstream: one level per
  frame, so an idle buffer could live 64 frames);
- an image or buffer allocation that fails, or would leave less than 48 MiB
  of direct memory, first waits for the GPU and frees idle staging buffers,
  then retries.
